# $HOME-relative paths replicated by the dotfiles component. This file is
# user-authored: `capture` reads it (never rewrites it) and copies each
# path into manifests/default/dotfiles/. Lines starting with ! remove
# already-captured payload (regenerable content); # starts a comment.
.vimrc
.vim
!.vim/plugged
.zprofile
.zshenv
.p10k.zsh
.oh-my-zsh/custom
.config/gh
.config/nvim
Library/Preferences/com.googlecode.iterm2.plist
# .zshrc is NOT captured yet: the capture-time secret scan flags it. Move
# any secret exports into an untracked ~/.zshrc.local, source that file
# from .zshrc, then uncomment the next line and re-run capture (the
# gitleaks gate will verify the result is clean):
# .zshrc
